{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774720,"nonce":"Hz9hAfHtEmsKt54MtgT4/sY6M+M=","title":"Helm dogfood durability + rollout, executor fail-fast, UI fixes, dev-env cleanup","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #38 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/helm-rerun-durability-and-ui` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-19T17:46:02Z · Merged: 2026-07-19T18:30:41Z\n\nBundles this session's fixes plus some pre-existing tree WIP (see last section).\n\n- **In-cluster MinIO** (`minio.yaml`, official images + PVC, no Bitnami). The dogfood had no S3, so the CAS ran on the server's `scratch` emptyDir — every restart wiped all workspaces, and any **rerun of a prior run hung forever at `Init:1/3`** (its input workspace was gone). `deploy.sh` now renders the S3 values and creates the bucket. Verified end-to-end: fresh manual run → rerun of a step now succeeds.\n- **Reliable image rollout.** Mutable tags (`edge`, `dogfood-local`) made `helm upgrade` a no-op, so a redeploy never restarted the Pod or pulled the new image. A per-deploy `DEPLOY_NONCE` pod annotation forces a fresh Pod each time.\n- **`just local-helm-ui`** — persistent port-forward that reconnects across Pod rolls.\n\nWhen a workspace input is missing from the CAS (`StorageError::NotFound`), `drive_workspace` now deletes the barrier-stuck Pod and fails the attempt (`Infra{never_started}`) with a clear message, instead of leaving `scarab-workspace-init` waiting forever.\n\n- **Doodle** no longer throws on an unknown motif (it was white-screening whole routes) — it degrades gracefully; added the missing `rocket` doodle.\n- **RunPipeline**: fixed a `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'inputs')` crash (guarded the interface read), and render the resolved SHA as a tidy commit chip.\n- **vite.config**: the dev server now requires `SCARAB_API_URL` (no silent default), scoped to `serve` — same-origin production builds are unaffected.\n\nRetired direnv/`.env.local` and the redundant `just server` recipe. One gitignored dev env file (`deploy/local-proc/.env`) seeded from a committed `.env.example`; recipes source it. `.env`/`.env.*` are now gitignored as a class (only `.env.example` templates are tracked).\n\n\u003e ⚠️ Retires the ADR-0036 cluster-free host-executor one-liner (`just server`). The capability still exists in the binary; say the word to re-add it as a self-contained recipe.\n\nThe `wip(brand): …` commit is uncommitted work that was already in the tree (ASCII page backdrops, beetle scenes, `RepoView` backdrop, regenerated assets) — **not** part of this session's fixes. Bundled per request; drop that commit or split it out if you'd rather it land separately.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}